def finding_html(f):
    refs=' · '.join(ref(r['path'],r['line']) for r in f['refs'])
    return f'''<article class="finding" data-level="{f['level']}"><div class="finding-top"><span class="severity {f['level'].lower()}">{f['level']}</span><span class="tag">{f['evidence']}</span><span class="finding-id">F{f['id']}</span></div><h3 id="finding-{f['id']}">{f['title']}</h3><p>{f['observed']}</p><div class="finding-detail"><div><h4>Why it matters</h4><p>{f['impact']}</p></div><div><h4>Improvement principle</h4><p>{f['principle']}</p></div></div><details><summary>Source evidence</summary><p class="source">{refs}</p></details></article>'''
report=f'''<section class="hero report-hero"><div class="eyebrow">08 / Architecture review</div><h1>A strong compiler foundation.<br><em>Uneven guarantees around it.</em></h1><p class="lede">The main opportunity is to make correctness, identity, state and evaluation consistent across the service. The project does not need a broad microservice expansion to address its most consequential weaknesses.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="#findings">Read the findings ↓</a><a class="button secondary" href="index.html">Open the teaching guide ↗</a></div><p class="snapshot">Snapshot <code>{COMMIT}</code><br>Review date: 09 November 2026 · Conclusions refer to this checkout.</p></section>
<section><div class="eyebrow">Design summary</div><h2>The architecture is sensible in outline.</h2><p>The frontend delegates over HTTP to a Python service. The service prefers deterministic translation, can retrieve saved examples, and can ask Gemini for fallback or repair. Local validators, live execution and optional result comparison aim to increase trust. Feedback can feed the reference corpus, cached context and model training.</p><p>The compiler extraction into typed IR, data-driven resolution and separate emitters is the clearest architectural strength. The weakest areas are the contracts between those layers: a review flag can be lost, missing validation can become success, and tenant-specific results can enter shared caches. The learning architecture is less complete than the synchronous translator.</p><div class="cards two"><article><h3>Preserve these strengths</h3><ul><li>Deterministic compiler and typed query representation.</li><li>Mapping data separated from language logic.</li><li>HTTP separation between Streamlit and backend.</li><li>Dependency injection and typed translation context as test seams.</li><li>Authentication middleware, admin checks, encrypted credential support, query guards and TLS verification.</li><li>Infrastructure intent: workload identities, Secret Manager, private VMs and explicit network controls.</li><li>A substantial local suite, including a passing compiler-specific suite.</li></ul></article><article><h3>Improve these design properties</h3><ul><li>Truthful validation states and preserved semantic uncertainty.</li><li>Tenant-scoped execution evidence and versioned caches.</li><li>One request/result contract across all API variants.</li><li>Durable ownership of feedback, jobs and knowledge revisions.</li><li>Independent evaluation with enforceable dataset isolation.</li><li>Executable deployment and training contracts.</li><li>Smaller orchestration responsibilities and observable failures.</li></ul></article></div></section>
<section><div class="eyebrow">Architectural tradeoffs</div><h2>Keep the core cohesive; separate work by lifecycle.</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Benefit</th><th>Cost / boundary to respect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Modular translation backend</td><td>Low-latency in-process compiler, resolver and validation calls; straightforward local tests.</td><td>Modules need typed contracts and explicit state ownership to avoid hidden coupling.</td></tr><tr><td>Deterministic first, AI when needed</td><td>Inspectable behavior for known constructs; flexibility for long-tail queries.</td><td>AI output must preserve constraints and receive the same evidence requirements.</td></tr><tr><td>Saved gold examples</td><td>Fast, repeatable answers for known queries.</td><td>Literal-preserving keys, provenance and independent held-out evaluation are essential.</td></tr><tr><td>Asynchronous learning workers</td><td>Training and corpus maintenance can run independently of request latency.</td><td>Requires durable artifacts, idempotent jobs and explicit promotion authority.</td></tr><tr><td>Live verification</td><td>Checks a real target environment.</td><td>Tenant identity, cost, time window, query limits and absent evidence must be explicit.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="callout"><b>Overall assessment</b><p>Useful and substantial engineering, especially in the compiler. The current checkout should not be treated as an end-to-end verified, automatically self-improving translation platform. The highest-value improvements strengthen the guarantees already advertised by the design.</p></div></section>
<section id="findings"><div class="eyebrow">Evidence-backed findings</div><h2>Where the design currently breaks its promises.</h2><p>Severity reflects review judgment about impact, not an official vulnerability score. “Reproduced” means exercised locally with synthetic inputs or test doubles; it does not mean a production incident was observed.</p><div class="filter-row" role="group" aria-label="Filter findings"><button class="active" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All 15</button><button data-filter="High" aria-pressed="false">High · 9</button><button data-filter="Medium" aria-pressed="false">Medium · 6</button></div><div id="finding-list">{''.join(finding_html(f) for f in findings)}</div></section>
<section><div class="eyebrow">Validation</div><h2>The compiler suite passed; the broader service suite did not.</h2><p><b>805 passed, 21 failed, 4 skipped</b> across local unit and compiler tests. Compiler-specific: 283 passed, 4 skipped. Eleven focused probes reproduced the behaviors described in the guide. The full failure count includes stale tests and shared-cache contamination, so it is not a count of distinct defects.</p><p>No live tenant, cloud tuning, deployment or Docker-build validation was performed. The original lockfile install failed on pywin32; tests used a separate Python 3.13 dependency set. This review combined repository-wide indexing, detailed tracing of critical flows, configuration analysis and controlled local execution.</p><a class="button secondary" href="index.html#evidence">Inspect results, probes and limitations →</a><div class="downloads"><a href="assets/findings.json" download>Download findings JSON ↓</a><button onclick="window.print()">Print architecture review / save PDF</button></div></section>'''
(ROOT/'architecture-review.html').write_text(shell('Architecture review',report,True))
print('Built two offline pages, seven SVG diagrams, findings and evidence assets.')
